I just discovered that if \tableofcontents (or one of its near
relatives) is in an \include'd file which is not included (because of
\includeonly) the table of contents is not updated. There are arguments
for both; personally I'd like to see it be updated since I use
\includeonly to reduce the amount of time it takes to get results back
>from a style file modification (and a quick peek at the toc file tells
me more than enough to get by).

-dh


